@import com.example.septic.data.model.ContentPage
@import com.example.septic.web.PageMeta
@import com.example.septic.web.RecordHelpEntry
@param PageMeta page
@param ContentPage contentPage
@template.layouts.app(page = page, designFamily = "editorial", pageStyles = "/record-problem-guide.css", content = @`
<div class="problem-guide">
    <section class="problem-hero"><div class="container problem-hero__inner">
        <div class="problem-hero__copy"><span class="eyebrow">Independent platform guide / Carmody</span><h1>Find your SepticSearch record.</h1><p class="lede">${contentPage.introCopy()}</p><a class="button button--primary" href="https://septicsearch.com/property-records" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="septicsearch_hero" data-track-target-type="official_lookup">Open SepticSearch ↗</a><a class="problem-text-link" href="#search-steps">Follow the search steps ↓</a><p>SepticPath is independent of SepticSearch, Carmody and government agencies.</p></div>
        <figure class="problem-plan"><img class="problem-plan__image" src="/images/studio/research-desk-v1.webp" width="1672" height="941" alt="Illustrative research desk with a property file" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Illustrative research materials—not a SepticSearch result or property record.</figcaption></figure>
    </div></section>
    <section class="section problem-body" id="search-steps"><div class="container problem-body__grid"><div>
        <span class="eyebrow">From search to source</span><h2>Find the record behind the result.</h2>
        <article class="problem-step"><span>01</span><div><h3>Select the state and county.</h3><p>Start with the property jurisdiction, not the owner’s mailing address. If your county is unavailable, use its official septic program to identify the correct system. This is not a complete national database.</p></div></article>
        <article class="problem-step"><span>02</span><div><h3>Try one useful identifier at a time.</h3><p>The current search offers last name, tax parcel ID, street and permit-related fields. For street-name searches, omit suffixes such as Street or Road; the street number is optional. Broaden an overly specific search, but do not treat a nearby result as the right property.</p></div></article>
        <article class="problem-step"><span>03</span><div><h3>Open the scanned documents.</h3><p>Compare the address, parcel or lot, permit number and document date on every page. Separate the application, approved design, installation record, final approval and later repairs. A service-history entry is not necessarily the original plan.</p><a href="/how-to-read-septic-as-built/">Read the drawing and approval together →</a></div></article>
        <article class="problem-step"><span>04</span><div><h3>Keep the missing item specific.</h3><p>No property result, no scanned drawing and no final approval are different gaps. Save the identifiers you searched and ask the responsible office for the missing existing file. An empty result is not an agency no-record response.</p><a href="/no-septic-records-found/">Continue after an empty search →</a></div></article>
        <div class="problem-example"><span class="eyebrow">Verified agency referral / Florida</span><h3>Franklin County links to SepticSearch.</h3><p>The Florida Department of Health in Franklin County lists the platform among its environmental-health resources. That referral does not guarantee a record for every property or establish coverage in other counties.</p><a href="https://franklin.floridahealth.gov/programs-and-services/environmental-health/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Check the official agency referral ↗</a><p><a href="/florida-ostds-permit-lookup/">Other Florida OSTDS lookup routes →</a> · <a href="/onlinerme-septic-records/">Agency sent you to OnlineRME instead? →</a></p></div>
    </div><aside class="problem-help"><span class="eyebrow">Stuck at the search?</span><h2>Send the address.<br>We’ll investigate.</h2><p>We check alternate identifiers and record sources, request the existing file when needed, and explain what the returned documents support.</p><a class="button button--primary" href="${RecordHelpEntry.of("missing").link("/septicsearch-records/")}" data-record-help-cta data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="septicsearch_missing" data-track-target-type="lead_form">Help find my record</a><p class="problem-help__terms">Free records and explanation. Agency fees need your approval. Agency response time controls files held only by that office.</p><a href="${RecordHelpEntry.of("review").link("/septicsearch-records/")}" data-record-help-cta data-track-click="nav" data-track-source-context="septicsearch_review" data-track-target-type="lead_form">Already have the file? Ask us to explain it →</a></aside></div></section>
    <section class="section problem-faq"><div class="container problem-body__grid"><div><h2>Before you rely on the result.</h2>@for(var faq : contentPage.faqBlocks())<details><summary>${faq.question()}</summary><p>${faq.answer()}</p></details>@endfor</div><div class="problem-sources"><h3>Sources and review</h3><p><a href="https://septicsearch.com/property-records" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SepticSearch: current search instructions</a></p><p><a href="https://septicsearch.com/faq" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SepticSearch: platform questions</a></p><p>Reviewed ${contentPage.reviewedAt()}. Search fields and county availability can change. This review checked the public instructions and search screen, not a successful search for a particular property.</p><p>A historical file does not establish current condition, exact field location or permission to build or dig.</p></div></div></section>
</div>
`)
